1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,020
Listen to talk in a physics class.

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:04,232
M:

3
00:00:04,232 --> 00:00:06,150
We've been talking about the law of inertia.

4
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:10,652
An object moving in a straight line will continue to move in a straight

5
00:00:10,652 --> 00:00:14,230
line unless it is acted upon by another force.

6
00:00:14,230 --> 00:00:17,070
So what does this mean in the real world?

7
00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:22,210
Let's look at something many people do all the time, riding a bicycle.

8
00:00:22,210 --> 00:00:25,100
Think about riding along in a straight line.

9
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:29,070
Once the bike is moving, inertia will keep it going in a straight line.

10
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:31,290
But we don't just ride in straight lines, do we?

11
00:00:31,290 --> 00:00:35,220
We turn at corners and steer around things that are in our way.

12
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:38,270
So how do you get the bicycle not to go straight?

13
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:40,064
Easy, right?

14
00:00:40,064 --> 00:00:43,290
Don't you just need to turn the front wheel in the direction you want to turn?

15
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:49,150
In fact, if you only turn the front wheel, you're likely to end up on the pavement.

16
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:50,383
The wheel will turn,

17
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:54,699
but because of inertia, your body and the rest of the bike will want

18
00:00:54,699 --> 00:00:56,240
to keep moving straight ahead.

19
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:59,363
So how does a cyclist avoid this?

20
00:00:59,363 --> 00:01:02,040
The key is to lean in.

21
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:05,070
Weight needs to shift in the direction of the turn

22
00:01:05,070 --> 00:01:09,010
so that the force of gravity can work against the force of inertia.

23
00:01:09,010 --> 00:01:14,125
Professional cyclists who move at high speeds need to hit a sweet spot, lean

24
00:01:14,125 --> 00:01:17,779
more to keep their bicycles from sliding out of turns,

25
00:01:17,779 --> 00:01:19,240
but not too much.

26
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:25,190
At a certain point, gravity will bring both rider and bicycle down to the ground.
